  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public private partnership Hub-ANDI Colombia 2016-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Public private partnership Hub-ANDI Colombia 2016-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution aims at improving sustainable economic situation of women and men that have been affected by the internal armed conflict facilitating the inclusion of their small scale production in the value chain of anchor companies, through inclusive and environmentally sustainable public-private partnerships.

Output 1: Small scale producers are strengthened and highly competitive and are engaged in inclusive and environmentally sustainable public-private partnerships.
Output 2: Business sector includes competitive raw materials from small scale producers, as suppliers in their value chain.
Output 3: The Hub is recognized by all stakeholders as an articulator platform that is able to facilitate inclusive business with real impact on improving the quality of life of the vulnerable population and with strong gender and environmental perspectives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ANDI FOUNDATION har ans&#xf6;kt till Sida om finansiering p&#xe5; 6,7 MSEK f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;rande av projektet &#x201c;Business in development facility Hub&#x201d; under perioden 1 juni 2016 till den 31 jan 2022.
Projektet syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra den ekonomiska situationen f&#xf6;r kvinnor och m&#xe4;n som drabbats av konfliken eller i konfliktdrabbade omr&#xe5;den genom att underl&#xe4;tta inf&#xf6;randet av sm&#xe5;skalig produktion i v&#xe4;rdekedjan hos ankar f&#xf6;retag, genom inkluderande och milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssigt h&#xe5;llbara partnerskap mellan den offentliga och den privata sektorn.

Den totala projektbudgeten &#xe4;r p&#xe5; 9,4 MSEK varav Sverige avser att bidra med 39%.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution is a program support to ANDI FOUNDATION that aims at improving sustainable economic situation of women and men that have been affected by the internal armed conflict facilitating the inclusion of their small-scale production in the value chain of anchor companies, through inclusive and environmentally sustainable public-private partnerships. The starting point is to create feasible long term commercial relations through the coordination of different public and private allies that help to reduce gaps between the supply from small scale producers and the demand of anchor companies. 

This is second phase of Sida&#x2019;s contribution 52060045.</narrative>
  </description>
